        # **Typed Uniforms, Inspector Groups, Palettes & Vulkan Layout Packing**: How nested uniform groups, doc comments, hex colors, palette arrays, and Vulkan std430/std140 layouts compile across GDShader and GLSL.
        #
        # CRShader unifies Godot Inspector ergonomics with Vulkan `RenderingDevice` descriptor layout rules from a single declaration syntax:
        # - **Inspector Groups & Doc Harvesting**: `group` / `subgroup` blocks emit balanced `group_uniforms Group.Subgroup;` directives, and `# comments` directly above uniforms emit `/** ... */` Godot Inspector tooltips.
        # - **Hex & Palette Resources**: `Color.hex("#rrggbb")` converts hex strings to normalized floats at compile time; `PackedColorArray[...]` and `resource("res://palette.tres")` synthesize `const int <name>_size = N;` plus typed uniform arrays.
        # - **Deterministic GLSL Layout Packing (`GLSLLayoutPacker`)**: When compiling to `.glsl`, opaque samplers receive non-colliding `set = 0, binding = N` slots, compact scalar/vector blocks (`<= 128` bytes, no arrays) pack into `layout(push_constant, std430) uniform CrShaderParams`, and array/large blocks automatically upgrade to `layout(set = 1, binding = 0, std140) uniform CrShaderUniforms`.
