        # **Declarative Shader Archetypes**: Zero-boilerplate domain blocks (sprite_effect, ui_effect, screen_effect, surface_material) that hoist uniforms and synthesize pipeline boilerplate.
        #
        # Archetypes eliminate repetitive Godot setup code while allowing `property`, `sampler`, `class`, and `def` declarations right inside the block:
        # - **`sprite_effect`**: Sets `shader_type canvas_item`, samples `TEXTURE * COLOR`, optionally exposes `TEXTURE_PIXEL_SIZE`, and binds the final expression to `COLOR`.
        # - **`ui_effect`**: Computes screen-space UV derivatives (`dFdx`/`dFdy`) so SDF circles, rings, and borders stay circular even on stretched non-square `Control` nodes.
        # - **`screen_effect`**: Supports both 2D `canvas_item` and 3D `mode: :spatial, depth: true` full-screen post-process quads (auto-emitting `POSITION = vec4(VERTEX.xy, 1.0, 1.0)`, `screen_texture`, and `depth_texture`).
        # - **`surface_material`**: Configures curated 3D `render_mode` presets (`:pbr`, `:toon`, `:glass`, `:foliage`, `:unshaded`).
        #
        # #### Side-by-Side Output Comparison
        #
        # <div class="jasper-comparison" style="width:100%;max-width:100%;margin:16px 0 24px;box-sizing:border-box;">
