        # **Composable shader_trait & Hygienic use_trait Fusion**: Fusing reusable vertex, fragment, light, and cross-target pixel traits with automatic prefix namespacing and AST local-variable hygiene.
        #
        # Unlike `#include` files (which cannot merge logic into `vertex()` or `fragment()` and collide when included twice), `shader_trait` and `use_trait` fuse modular effects at the AST level:
        # - **Cross-Target `on_pixel` Hooks**: Built-in post-processing traits (`vignette`, `chromatic_aberration`, `color_grade`, `film_grain`, `shockwave_ripple`) compile seamlessly into **both** 2D/3D `.gdshader` screen passes (`texture(screen_texture, ...)`) and Godot 4.8 Vulkan `.glsl` compositor passes (`imageLoad(color_image, ...)`).
        # - **Multi-Instance `prefix:` Namespacing & Hygiene**: Applying the same trait twice (`prefix: :key` and `prefix: :fill`) namespaces every uniform, group, constant, struct, helper, and stage-local variable (`_key_rim_fresnel_f1_0_ndotv`) so local declarations never collide.
